    rationale:
      "With NEXT_STEPS still fully gated (all five items operator/legal/infra-blocked, independently reconfirmed via mcp__github__actions_list that github-actions-runner-unavailable is still accurate - the 10 most recent workflow runs across all six scheduled-agent workflows plus pr-checks.yml all show status completed / conclusion failure), audited the same-day Growth-to-Complete upsell feature (growth-upsell-nudge, already independently reviewed once as clean in growth-upsell-audit-and-eslint-devdep-advisory-noted) against src/lib/orders/recurring.ts's own file-level invariant: \"sold monthly capabilities must ignore canceled rows.\" Found the prior audit's clean verdict missed a real gap: isGrowthOrder (src/lib/billing/growth-upsell.ts) - the positive \"has a live Growth order to upgrade from\" check underlying leadEligibleForGrowthUpsell, listGrowthUpsellCandidates, and oldestGrowthUpsellCandidateAgeHours alike - excluded a refunded or disputed Growth order but never checked orders.recurringCanceledAt (set by the Stripe webhook's customer.subscription.deleted handler). A lead whose Growth subscription had already been canceled therefore stayed a live candidate everywhere this feature surfaces: the pipeline-health growthUpsellCandidatesCount MetricCard, the daily-digest section, and the leads-client.tsx 'Growth -> Complete upsell' due-queue panel and per-row 'Upsell to Complete' button all kept treating a churned $99/mo subscriber as a $199/mo upgrade candidate.\n\nThis is a real customer-facing correctness bug, not just a metrics-visibility gap: sendGrowthUpsellAction's own leadEligibleForGrowthUpsell re-check happens against fresh data immediately before sending, so an operator clicking the button for a canceled subscriber would trigger sendGrowthUpsellEmail's actual copy ('Your marketing is already running on Growth') straight to a customer whose subscription had, in fact, already ended - false and potentially embarrassing after the very same day's subscription-canceled-win-back-notice shipped specifically to acknowledge that same cancellation gracefully. It also invites a confusing purchase flow: buildGrowthUpsellCheckoutPath links to a brand-new /checkout?tier=complete Session rather than resuming or referencing the lapsed Growth subscription, so a canceled subscriber clicking through gets a plain new Complete purchase with none of the 'upgrade, setup already covered' framing the email promises.\n\nisStarterOnlyOrder (the Starter-upsell sibling this module was modeled on) does not have the analogous gap - Starter is a one-time purchase with no Stripe Subscription to cancel, so recurringCanceledAt is structurally irrelevant there; the omission is specific to growth-upsell.ts's Growth-tier check, not a pattern needing the same fix elsewhere.\n\nFixed isGrowthOrder to additionally require !orderRecurringIsCanceled(order) (src/lib/orders/recurring.ts, already the established helper the sold-capability-entitlement family uses for this exact check), and threaded recurringCanceledAt through the type signatures of leadEligibleForGrowthUpsell's ordersForLead, listGrowthUpsellCandidates' orders, and oldestGrowthUpsellCandidateAgeHours' orders parameters so the field is explicit at every call site's type rather than only working by incidental structural-typing overlap with OrderRecord (which already carries recurringCanceledAt at runtime via listOrdersByLeadSlug - the actual bug was in the eligibility logic itself, not a missing field on the data). hasCompleteOrder (the negative 'already has Complete, never re-pitch' check) was deliberately left untouched - it already ignores refund/dispute status by design (mirroring starter-upsell's own documented reasoning: once sold, never re-pitch, regardless of what happened to that charge afterward), and a canceled-Complete lead should stay excluded from a Growth-upsell nudge for the identical reason.\n\nsrc/lib/billing/growth-upsell.ts - the fix (isGrowthOrder + three downstream type signatures) and updated doc comments. src/lib/billing/growth-upsell.test.ts - 6 new cases across isGrowthOrder / leadEligibleForGrowthUpsell / listGrowthUpsellCandidates / oldestGrowthUpsellCandidateAgeHours proving the exclusion, including a case confirming a lead with BOTH a stale canceled Growth order and a separate still-active one stays eligible (an old cancel followed by a fresh resubscribe checkout). src/app/dashboard/leads/send-growth-upsell-action.test.ts - 1 new action-level case proving sendGrowthUpsellAction itself now rejects a canceled-Growth lead with the standard eligibility error before ever calling sendGrowthUpsellEmail. Verified all 5 new/modified assertions actually catch the regression: git stash'd growth-upsell.ts's source change alone and confirmed all 5 failed (2 in growth-upsell.test.ts's other describe blocks also flipped as a side effect of the same stash) before restoring the fix. pipeline-health.test.ts and daily-digest.test.ts needed no changes - both already delegate entirely to listGrowthUpsellCandidates, and their existing fixtures carry no recurringCanceledAt so continue to pass unchanged; the fix's coverage lives at the layer that owns the logic, matching this codebase's established test-layering convention.\n\nAlso relevant given sibling PR #927's own finding (stripe-checkout-recurring-upgrade-dedup, merged just before this one): that fix makes an upsell checkout for an already-subscribed lead reuse the existing Stripe Customer and cancel the superseded subscription server-side — this canceled-exclusion fix is what stops that same lead from being re-offered the SAME upsell again afterward once recurringCanceledAt lands on the old (now-superseded) order; the two fixes are complementary, not overlapping, and were independently discovered.\n\nNo NEXT_STEPS change - the five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked, unchanged. File-size check per AGENT_PROTOCOL's re-archive note: prompt_process.tsx (~192KB) and business-decisions.ts (~244KB before this entry) both measured via wc -c - business-decisions.ts remains the closer of the two to the 262,144-byte trigger; the next session appending a sizeable entry to it should re-check rather than assume, and may need to run the re-archive as its own dedicated iteration soon.\n\nVerified: npm ci (413 packages) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run targeted (growth-upsell.test.ts + send-growth-upsell-action.test.ts + pipeline-health.test.ts + daily-digest.test.ts, 263/263 passed) then full suite (3748 passed, 217 files - up from 3741/217 pre-iteration baseline, +7 net new) + a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same 61-route split, no new warnings). No dev-server smoke check needed - server-only eligibility-logic fix with no new UI surface, exercised fully by the automated test suite; the existing leads-client.tsx panel and dashboard action are unchanged beyond the shared predicate they already call.",
